    rce-010: pickle.loads — logic_gap
      Create a malicious pickle file (e.g., exploit.pkl) that executes a reverse
shell. Send a POST request to /api/v1/trigger with untrusted_user_input pointing
to the path of exploit.pkl. The server will deserialize the pickle and execute 
the payload.
    rce-011: pickle.loads — logic_gap
      An attacker can craft a malicious pickle file and provide its path to 
`parse_file` with `allow_pickle=True`. The pickle payload can execute arbitrary 
commands, e.g., via `__reduce__`.
